berkeley-master.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: A1: it takes "unconceived" from imagining them as existing with no one at all conceiving them, which is the content of the thought to their being unconceived by you while you conceive them, which is a fact about your act, a reader says: the argument holds only through it; without it, C1 (S5) does not follow (berkeley-master.logic.r2.sense1)
berkeley-master.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C1 (S5): conceive_mind_indep = T, conceive_unconceived = T, repugnant = T
